[ARCHITECT] Build and verify one small reusable self-prompt helper for the visible LocalCoder Drone. This is bounded coding work; no daemon, schedule, journal write, or training.

[QUEEN → DRONE] Use the Monologue only as the agenda → verified evidence → next bounded action shape. First emit a concise visible `[DRONE SELF-PROMPT]` naming this function and its check. Then add exactly one new file, `workspace/autonomy/opencode_drone_prompts.py`, using `localcoder_add_python`. Implement one function `format_drone_self_prompt(agenda: str, verified_facts: str, next_action: str) -> str` that validates all three inputs are non-empty strings after whitespace trimming and returns a concise multi-line prompt beginning `[DRONE SELF-PROMPT]` with labeled Agenda, Verified facts, and Next bounded action fields. The docstring must say the helper formats only caller-supplied facts; it does not verify truth or grant authority. No other file changes.

After the add tool completes, self-prompt once with the actual verified result and one unmet requirement. Then call `shell` exactly once with `L:\.venv\Scripts\python.exe -B -c "import ast,pathlib; p=pathlib.Path('workspace/autonomy/opencode_drone_prompts.py'); src=p.read_text(encoding='utf-8'); ast.parse(src); ns={}; exec(compile(src,str(p),'exec'),ns); f=ns['format_drone_self_prompt']; out=f('bounded helper','AST parsed and imported','report verified output'); assert out.startswith('[DRONE SELF-PROMPT]'); assert 'Verified facts: AST parsed and imported' in out; assert 'Next bounded action: report verified output' in out; print(out); print('PASS: valid prompt structure');
try: f(' ','fact','action')
except ValueError: print('PASS: empty agenda rejected')
else: raise AssertionError('empty agenda accepted')"`. Do not retry either tool. Final response starts `[DRONE]`, reports the real verification output and any failures.

